Error [jet.DuplicateDefinition]: `expand: fn` is defined twice in `impl Marker`
  --> tests/ui/marker_impl_rejected_members.jet:13:9
    |
 13 |         expand: fn(self, target: Target) {}
    |         ^^^^^^
 Why: A marker has one template
 Fix: Remove one of the definitions
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0105

Error [jet.TraitMethodMismatch]: `render` is not a method of `Marker`
  --> tests/ui/marker_impl_rejected_members.jet:15:9
    |
 15 |         render: fn(self) {}
    |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: `impl Marker` has one method, the template the compiler expands with the marked item bound to `target`
 Fix: Write `expand: fn(self, target: Target) { … }`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0907

Error [jet.DuplicateTraitImpl]: `Traced` has a second `impl Marker` block
  --> tests/ui/marker_impl_rejected_members.jet:18:5
    |
 18 |     impl Marker {
    |     ^^^^
 Why: A struct declares one marker, so its settings, group and template share one block
 Fix: Move these members into the first `impl Marker` block
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0908

Error [jet.StackedRuleLines]: The marker group `Traced` has fields, settings or a template
  --> tests/ui/marker_impl_rejected_members.jet:4:1
    |
  4 | Traced: struct {
    | ^^^^^^
 Why: A group names a fixed marker stack, so a use site passes nothing into it and it expands to its members
 Fix: Remove everything but `group: #[…]`, or declare a marker without a group
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0999
